  "definitions": {
    "controls": "The restricted controls: age_band is the positive control (the planted effects of the filing-age band on the failure-to-appear log-odds and the next-filing exponent, which no model feature carries); synthetic_group is the negative control (drawn on its own stream after the persons; no draw reads it).",
    "courts": "Per court: the case-weighted mean of each effect over the judges who drew its judicial discretionary release decisions (each judge weighted by those decisions), the value p0 substitutes for the deciding judge's effect.",
    "judges": "Per judge: the courts it served, its planted leniency (release log-odds), new_case_effect (next-filing skew exponent), fta_effect (failure-to-appear log-odds), and docket_tilt (assignment log-weight per unit of risk index), and under centered each effect minus the decision-weighted mean of its courts' means (the effect the ratios rank). decisions_by_court counts the judicial discretionary release decisions the generator drew for the judge per court (the weights).",
    "parameters": "Every constant of the generator's functional forms (docs/SYNTHETIC_DATA.md \"Planted effects\"): the judge-effect ranges, the risk features and their numeric codes, the risk-index weights, the release, failure-to-appear, and next-filing forms, and the age effects by filing-age band.",
    "targets.pretrial_release": "Per judge, over the attributed judicial discretionary pretrial decisions (metrics.json pretrial.decisions): decisions, released (detained = false), expected = sum over the decisions of p = logistic(base + leniency) x the chance the release takes effect before the corpus end, expected_centered = the same sum with the court's mean leniency (p0), oracle_ratio = released / expected_centered, true_ratio = expected / expected_centered.",
    "targets.windowed": "new_case and failure_to_appear, per window w and judge, over the pretrial_release cohort of metrics.json (index_events.pretrial_release.windows.<w>): cohort, followed, observed (the fixed-window numerator), expected and expected_centered summed over the followed members, oracle_ratio = observed / expected_centered, true_ratio = expected / expected_centered. A member's p is the probability of its outcome in (exposure_start, exposure_start + w days] under the generator's draws given the realized exposure start. new_case: 0 without a next case; else the chance the next filing (earliest day + int(U ** k x (span + 1)) days, a business-hour minute, k = max(floor, base_exponent + the releasing judge's effect)) falls in the window, plus the chance it falls before the exposure start times whether a later case was filed in the window. failure_to_appear: 1 - (1 - q) x (1 - o), q = logistic(base + the judge's fta_effect) x the chance its date (the rule's hearing, or a uniform day and minute) falls in the window, o = 1 when another case of the person records a failure to appear in the window. p0 substitutes the court's mean effect for the judge's."
  },
